Let a python3 Gradle property name the Python that builds the wheels.

findPython3() takes the first supported Python it can run, trying the py
launcher before python3 and python. On Windows that is any Python the
machine happens to have, ahead of the one on the PATH; -Ppython3=python
pins the build to MSYS2's.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments

--- a/build.gradle
+++ b/build.gradle
@@ -251,6 +251,9 @@
 
 	def pyCmds = supportedVersions.collectMany { [["python$it"], ["py", "-$it"]] }
 	pyCmds += [['python3'], ['python'], ['py']]
+	if (findProperty("python3")) {
+		pyCmds = [[findProperty("python3")]]
+	}
 	for (pyCmd in pyCmds) {	
 		def pyVer = checkPythonVersion(pyCmd)
 		def pyExe = getPythonExecutable(pyCmd)
